description:
Write both ends of lesson 4.03's `IOCTL_LOG_READ` request: the viewer builds it, the driver validates it and works out how many 32-byte records fit in the reply.

```cpp
using NTSTATUS = std::int32_t;
constexpr NTSTATUS STATUS_SUCCESS = 0;
constexpr NTSTATUS STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER = static_cast<NTSTATUS>(0xC000000Du);
constexpr NTSTATUS STATUS_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL = static_cast<NTSTATUS>(0xC0000023u);

std::vector<std::uint8_t> buildReadRequest(std::uint64_t afterSeq);       // { u32 size = 16; u32 reserved = 0; u64 afterSeq }
NTSTATUS validateReadRequest(const std::uint8_t* input, std::uint32_t inLength, std::uint32_t outLength, std::uint64_t& afterSeq);
std::uint32_t recordsThatFit(std::uint32_t outLength);
```

`validateReadRequest`, in this order: input shorter than 16 bytes, or output shorter than the 16-byte reply header → `STATUS_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL`; `size` not 16 or `reserved` not 0 → `STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER`; otherwise `afterSeq` is set and the result is success. `recordsThatFit` is how many whole 32-byte records follow the 16-byte header (0 if not even the header fits).

